WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:01.650
- I didn't bring you here
just to sip some tea,

00:00:01.650 --> 00:00:02.800
I wanted to spill some tea.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:03.973
So I thought of a game.

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:06.660
I like to call it, "Sip It and Spill It"

00:00:06.660 --> 00:00:08.850
and it's basically a very
sophisticated version

00:00:08.850 --> 00:00:09.940
of "Never Have I Ever".

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:11.020
So I'm trying to keep something

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:13.230
very American and trashy, classy.

00:00:13.230 --> 00:00:15.190
But for example, sip it and spill it

00:00:15.190 --> 00:00:17.580
if you've ever locked
yourself in a bathroom

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:19.150
with a glass of wine
because you have children

00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:20.620
and you just want a minute to yourself.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.770
See, then I would take this bad boy

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.030
and I'd drink the whole thing.

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:25.411
- I'd have to drink that
with ya, I'm afraid.

00:00:25.411 --> 00:00:26.530
(group laughs)

00:00:26.530 --> 00:00:27.363
- I'm like, I just need,
- Sorry.

00:00:27.363 --> 00:00:29.520
- "Mommy needs a minute."
- Yeah.

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:30.563
- Okay, I have one!

00:00:31.410 --> 00:00:34.440
Sip it and spill it, if
you've ever rolled Easter eggs

00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:36.531
while wearing a bonnet and dress.

00:00:36.531 --> 00:00:39.850
(pensive music)

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:41.250
(chimes ringing)

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:42.149
- It's you!

00:00:42.149 --> 00:00:43.483
(group laughs)

00:00:43.483 --> 00:00:46.210
You wear a bonnet often?
(silverware drops)

00:00:46.210 --> 00:00:47.180
Oh my god.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:48.990
- It was Easter. My friend
said, "Put on a dress

00:00:48.990 --> 00:00:51.150
and let's roll the Easter egg
down the hill," so we did.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.022
- This makes you my
favorite person at the table

00:00:53.022 --> 00:00:53.855
(group laughs)
once again.

00:00:53.855 --> 00:00:54.688
- You said that twice.

00:00:54.688 --> 00:00:56.110
- I know, once again.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.590
- Okay, wait. Hugh, your turn.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:00.630
- Sip it and spill it, if
you've ever snogged Brad Pitt.

00:01:00.630 --> 00:01:01.995
- Snogged means kissed right?

00:01:01.995 --> 00:01:02.828
- Kissed. Kissed.

00:01:02.828 --> 00:01:03.661
- Are you about to sip your tea?

00:01:03.661 --> 00:01:04.494
- Shall I show you?

00:01:04.494 --> 00:01:06.102
Well I'm just going to, you know, just...

00:01:06.102 --> 00:01:06.935
(chimes ringing)

00:01:06.935 --> 00:01:07.768
Go Elizabeth!

00:01:07.768 --> 00:01:08.726
- What is that story?

00:01:08.726 --> 00:01:10.120
(audience applauds)

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:11.615
- Somebody had to.

00:01:11.615 --> 00:01:13.433
- Somebody had to sacrifice.

00:01:13.433 --> 00:01:15.690
- Well I did it as a paid job,

00:01:15.690 --> 00:01:17.050
because we were on a set, acting in--

00:01:17.050 --> 00:01:18.520
- What a beautifully paid job.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.364
- Yes, indeed. There are
worse ways to earn a living.

00:01:21.364 --> 00:01:22.197
- Wow

00:01:22.197 --> 00:01:23.030
- So I was not complaining, but yeah.

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.659
He cut his teeth with me
I think, yeah as it were.

00:01:25.659 --> 00:01:26.647
- Nice, did you teach
him how to snog well?

00:01:26.647 --> 00:01:28.770
- I made him the man that he is.

00:01:28.770 --> 00:01:30.260
- You made him a good snogger?

00:01:30.260 --> 00:01:31.730
- Yes, he's learned everything from me.

00:01:31.730 --> 00:01:33.520
- I always loved that y'all call it that.

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:34.353
- [Allen] Snogging.

00:01:34.353 --> 00:01:35.480
- 'Cause it sounds not cool.

